---
// Accessibility Statement Page
import Layout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Accessibility Statement" 
  description="Smiths Lake Village website accessibility commitment and compliance information"
>
  <style>
    .accessibility-page {
      background: #f7f9fc;
      padding: 3rem 0;
    }

    .page-header {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1B365D 0%, #2B4A7D 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: 4rem 1rem 3rem;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .page-header h1 {
      color: white;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .page-header p {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 1rem 4rem;
    }

    .content-section {
      background: white;
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    }

    .content-section h2 {
      color: #1B365D;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
      border-bottom: 3px solid #F5A623;
    }

    .content-section h3 {
      color: #1B365D;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
    }

    .content-section p {
      color: #374151;
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .content-section ul {
      margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
      color: #374151;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .content-section li {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .compliance-badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      background: #10B981;
      color: white;
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 1rem 0;
    }

    .contact-box {
      background: #F7F9FC;
      border-left: 4px solid #5B9BD5;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin: 2rem 0;
    }

    .contact-box h3 {
      color: #1B365D;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .contact-box a {
      color: #5B9BD5;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .contact-box a:hover {
      color: #1B365D;
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .standards-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .standards-table th {
      background: #1B365D;
      color: white;
      padding: 1rem;
      text-align: left;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .standards-table td {
      padding: 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #E5E7EB;
    }

    .standards-table tr:last-child td {
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .feature-list {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .feature-item {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      background: #F7F9FC;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .feature-icon {
      color: #10B981;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .page-header h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .content-section {
        padding: 1.5rem;
      }

      .feature-list {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="accessibility-page">
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p>
        The Pacific Palms Community Association is committed to ensuring digital accessibility 
        for all community members and visitors.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-container">
      
      <!-- Commitment Section -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          The Smiths Lake Village website (villagefirst.org.au) is designed to be accessible to 
          people of all abilities, including those using assistive technologies. We are committed 
          to providing an inclusive digital experience that enables everyone to access community 
          information, services, and resources.
        </p>
        <div class="compliance-badge">
          ✓ WCAG 2.1 Level AA Compliant
        </div>
        <p>
          This website has been developed to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 
          2.1 at Level AA standard, as recommended by the Australian Government Digital Service 
          Standard.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Accessibility Features -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Accessibility Features</h2>
        <p>We have implemented the following features to ensure accessibility:</p>

        <div class="feature-list">
          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Keyboard Navigation</strong>
              <p>Full keyboard access to all interactive elements</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Screen Reader Support</strong>
              <p>Semantic HTML and ARIA labels throughout</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Text Alternatives</strong>
              <p>Alt text for all meaningful images</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Color Contrast</strong>
              <p>WCAG AA compliant color ratios</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Responsive Design</strong>
              <p>Mobile-friendly layouts on all devices</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Clear Headings</strong>
              <p>Logical heading structure for navigation</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Focus Indicators</strong>
              <p>Visible focus states for all interactive elements</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <span class="feature-icon">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Skip Links</strong>
              <p>Quick navigation to main content</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Standards Compliance -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Standards & Compliance</h2>
        <p>This website conforms to the following standards:</p>

        <table class="standards-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Standard</th>
              <th>Compliance Level</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1</td>
              <td><strong>Level AA</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Australian Government Digital Service Standard</td>
              <td><strong>Compliant</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Disability Discrimination Act 1992</td>
              <td><strong>Compliant</strong></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Known Limitations -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          While we strive for full accessibility, some limitations may exist:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Third-party content:</strong> Some embedded maps, videos, or external documents 
            may not meet accessibility standards. We are working with providers to improve accessibility.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>PDF documents:</strong> Older PDF documents may not be fully accessible. 
            We are progressively reviewing and updating these documents.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Historical content:</strong> Some archive materials may have limited accessibility 
            due to their original format and age.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you encounter any accessibility barriers, please contact us (details below) so we can 
          address them promptly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Assistive Technologies -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Supported Assistive Technologies</h2>
        <p>This website has been tested with the following assistive technologies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>NVDA (Windows)</li>
          <li>JAWS (Windows)</li>
          <li>VoiceOver (macOS, iOS)</li>
          <li>TalkBack (Android)</li>
          <li>Keyboard-only navigation</li>
          <li>Browser zoom up to 200%</li>
          <li>High contrast mode</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Browser Compatibility -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Browser Compatibility</h2>
        <p>This website is designed to work with current versions of:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Chrome</li>
          <li>Mozilla Firefox</li>
          <li>Microsoft Edge</li>
          <li>Apple Safari</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For the best experience, we recommend using the latest version of your preferred browser.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Feedback and Contact -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Feedback and Support</h2>
        <p>
          We welcome feedback on the accessibility of the Smiths Lake Village website. 
          If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, 
          please contact us:
        </p>

        <div class="contact-box">
          <h3>Accessibility Coordinator</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="/contact">via our contact form</a><br>
            <strong>Response time:</strong> We aim to respond within 5 business days
          </p>
          <p>
            When reporting an accessibility issue, please include:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>The web page URL where you experienced the issue</li>
            <li>A description of the problem</li>
            <li>Your browser and operating system</li>
            <li>Any assistive technology you were using</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ongoing Improvements -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Ongoing Improvements</h2>
        <p>
          Accessibility is an ongoing commitment. We regularly review and update our website 
          to ensure it remains accessible and user-friendly for all visitors.
        </p>
        <h3>Recent Updates</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>November 2025:</strong> Website redesign with WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance</li>
          <li><strong>December 2025:</strong> Added skip navigation links</li>
          <li><strong>January 2026:</strong> Enhanced keyboard navigation and focus indicators</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Planned Improvements</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Progressive PDF accessibility review and updates</li>
          <li>Additional language support options</li>
          <li>Enhanced multimedia accessibility (captions, transcripts)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Statement Date -->
      <div class="content-section">
        <h2>Statement Information</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Statement prepared:</strong> January 2026<br>
          <strong>Last reviewed:</strong> January 17, 2026<br>
          <strong>Next review:</strong> July 2026
        </p>
        <p>
          This accessibility statement applies to the Smiths Lake Village website 
          (villagefirst.org.au) operated by the Pacific Palms Community Association (PPCA).
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
